minios-configurator (3.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Use minios-gui 1.1.0 shared HeaderBar, StatusBanner, token-aware completion,
    and keyboard-accessible contextual Help popovers.
  * Adopt shared styling, dialogs, and icon handling from minios-gui.
  * Move password visibility controls into the password entries.
  * Confirm before discarding unsaved changes.
  * Prevent edits and detection actions while an asynchronous detection or save
    is running, avoiding a race that could mark an unpersisted edit as saved.
  * Keep temporary-path test fixtures compatible with Bionic's pytest 3.3.
  * Require the OpenSSH 7.6-compatible security and live-config packages.

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0300

minios-configurator (3.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Redesign the configurator as a non-linear, category-based application with
    change tracking, reset, and a password-redacted review before saving.
  * Add security profiles for common security postures.
  * Distinguish inherited values, effective defaults, and explicit edits so
    unchanged defaults are not written to the configuration.
  * Detect current system and keyboard settings without blocking the interface
    or saving detected values automatically.
  * Add inline and cross-field validation for account, service, security, and
    user-media settings.
  * Show whether settings apply after reboot or only when creating a new
    session, and document user-media, migration, toram, and log-export behavior.
  * Preserve configuration comments, ordering, unknown keys, ownership,
    permissions, and extended attributes while rejecting symlinks and
    non-regular files and saving atomically.
  * Recognize SysV services and canonical systemd boot targets, and report LUKS
    persistence availability from the running initrd capability marker.
  * Adopt the compact MiniOS application style, add visible per-setting help,
    and update documentation and translations.

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0300

